    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>Weapon (Warhammer), Artifact (Requires Attunement by a Barbarian)</em></p><p>Long ago on the world of Draenor, an orc named Gelnar set out to fashion a weapon that would empower his people against their ogre foes. He forged a fearsome hammer in the heat of an elemental pool of lava. Dubbed <em>Doomhammer</em>, this weapon was passed down through generations of Blackrock orcs. An ancient prophecy foretold that possession of the hammer would someday leave the Blackrock lineage; this prophecy came true when Thrall, an orc shaman, proved himself the weapon’s worthy wielder.</p><p><strong>Magic Weapon.</strong> You gain a +3 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls made with this magic weapon. It deals an extra 1d8 Lightning damage on a hit.</p><p><strong>Gelnar’s Gifts.</strong> While holding <em>Doomhammer</em>, you gain the following benefits:</p><ul><li><p><strong>Doom Winds.</strong> Your fury carries the unbridled momentum of a windstorm. While your Rage is active, your Speed is doubled, and you can take an extra Attack action (one attack only) on each of your turns.</p></li><li><p><strong>Lava Stride.</strong> You take no damage from molten lava and can walk across it as if it were solid ground.</p></li><li><p><strong>Lightning Rod.</strong> When a creature you can see within 60 feet of you would take Lightning damage, you can take a Reaction to reduce the damage to 0.</p></li><li><p><strong>Storm’s Passage.</strong> You can cast @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplWindWalk00]{Wind Walk} from this weapon. Once the weapon has been used to cast this spell, it can’t be used to cast it again until the next dawn.</p></li></ul><p><strong>Random Properties.</strong> Doomhammer has the following random properties:</p><ul><li><p>2 minor beneficial properties</p></li><li><p>1 major beneficial property</p></li><li><p>1 minor detrimental property</p></li></ul><p><strong>Destroying Doomhammer.</strong> To destroy <em>Doomhammer</em>, a descendant of Gelnar must hurl the weapon into the eye of a storm in Outland, the remnants of the destroyed world of Draenor.</p><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-M5mTtyvl8ygsAX3o\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p>Quand votre Rage commence, appliquez l’effet <em>Doom Winds</em> (vitesse doublée) et retirez-le à sa fin ; l’attaque supplémentaire est à prendre vous-même. Pour <em>Lightning Rod</em>, annulez vous-même les dégâts de foudre. Les propriétés aléatoires d’artefact sont à ajouter par le MJ.</p></section>",
      "chat": ""
    },
